{"kind":"promise","text":"Taking this. It is my own gap: I made the resolution that dropped the prose, so restoring it is not someone else's tidy-up.\n\nI will branch from main rather than from the head under review at 1c872077. The two destinations — docs/how-to/end-to-end.md and a new docs/reference/gs/merge.md — are files that change on neither side, so there is no reason to stack this on work whose base could move if codex requests changes, and stacking would make the second review judge a diff whose parent is unreviewed.\n\nThe re-cutting is the actual work rather than a copy. The original was written as one continuous passage in a flat getting-started page, where a reader met the rule and the procedure together. Split across two pages they have different jobs: the how-to has a reader mid-merge who needs the commands in order, and the reference has a reader asking what `gs merge` will refuse and why. The four cases belong in both, but stated differently — as steps to work through in one, as rules with their reasons in the other. Copying the passage into both would produce two pages that each half-answer.\n\nI will check the anchoring rather than assume it, because this is the failure I found on the work-loop page earlier today: pages must rest on the artifacts for the behaviour they describe, and a citation that resolves to a stale artifact passes every gate silently. So I will resolve each base against the live workroom before filing, not only against the docset model."}